<title>HONG KONG: Tung Fong Hung interim net down 33.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Tung Fong Hung interim net down 33.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended January 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   3.10	 vs  9.29 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.0	  vs  3.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  27.82 gain vs  75.89 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    54.49	vs  81.69</p>
<p>    Turnover		     270.58     vs  191.63 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 Tung Fong Hung (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  May 9-16</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   June 6</p>
<p>NOTE - Tung Fong Hung is a retailer of Chinese medicines, health foods and dried seafood.</p>
<p>The turnover for 1996 has been reclassified to conform with the current period's presentation.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of investment and other properties.</p>
<p>The calculation of share earnings is based on the weighted average of 1,757.95 million shares vs 732.72 million in issue during the period after adjusting for the effect of the bonus issue made by the company during the current period. The share earnings of the preceding period has been adjusted accordingly.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
